{% extends "@Contao/content_element/_base.html.twig" %}

{#
    The basket (specification 4.2).

    Variables: notice (CartNotice or null), lines (list of {itemId, articleId,
    title, sku, position, quantity, lineGross, terms — a subscription's
    conditions or null, renews — the number of the subscription a renewal
    line continues, or '' (Abo-7b)}), unpriced (list of {itemId, articleId, title, sku,
    position, quantity}), total (formatted), is_empty (bool),
    account_required (bool — a subscription line and nobody signed in, Abo-2),
    checkout_url (string or null), checkout_blocked (bool — the checkout is
    blocked, so no link but its sentence, E4).

    All amounts arrive formatted — MoneyFormatter did the rounding and the
    currency, not this file (a template that rounds rounds differently from the
    order). The quantities arrive without their trailing zeros ("3", not
    "3.0000") and with a decimal POINT, because they go into input fields that
    are posted back and parsed as decimals.

    ⚠️ ONE FORM PER LINE, and each of them inside a <td>.

    A browser submits every field of the form the button belongs to. One form
    around the table would send the `item` of every line at once and the server
    would read the last one — the visitor changes a line they never touched.
    Moving the id onto the button (value="update:42") fixes only half of it:
    the `quantity` fields of the other lines still travel along. And a <form>
    may not be a child of <table>, <tbody> or <tr> — the parser moves it out
    and the fields end up in no form at all. A <td> takes flow content, so a
    form that lives wholly inside one cell is both valid and scoped to its line.

    ⚠️ ids are per ELEMENT and per LINE.

    Two basket elements can stand on one page, and each has several lines. The
    content element's own id (data.id) makes the instance unique, the line id
    makes the row unique — the same pattern as quantity_id in
    consho_product_detail.html.twig, one level deeper.

    The quantity field is type="text" with inputmode="decimal", not
    type="number": 0 is a legitimate entry here (it removes the line), and a
    min= that forbade it would have the browser refuse the very entry the
    server is meant to act on.

    ⚠️ EVERY line carries a mark, and it is VISIBLE.

    The title alone does not identify a line: CartTitles hands out the MAIN
    product's title by design, so two variants of one product read alike, and
    two lines with no title at all share one replacement text. That is not a
    screen reader's problem alone — a sighted visitor faces the same two rows
    and the same two "remove" buttons, which is why the mark stands in the row
    rather than in an aria-label nobody can see. The item number is the shop's
    own answer; where none is maintained it is the line's position in the
    basket, counted through both loops by the controller.

    The mark goes into the accessible name too (line_name), because the label
    of the quantity field and the text of both buttons are read out of context,
    away from the row they sit in.
#}

{% block content %}
    {% set field_prefix = 'consho-cart-' ~ data.id|default('') %}

    {% if notice %}
        <p class="consho-cart__notice" role="status">
            {{ ("CONSHO.cart.notice." ~ notice.value)|trans({}, "contao_default") }}
        </p>
    {% endif %}

    {#
        The age rating of the whole cart (C19): the highest over all
        lines, also over those without a price. It blocks nothing — 6, 12 and
4 are only a notice by definition, 16 and 18 are held up by the
        checkout, where there is an identity to check. It stands here so that a
        customer learns it before the address form and not after.
    #}
    {% if minimum_age|default(0) > 0 %}
        <p class="consho-cart__age" role="note">{{ "CONSHO.minimumAge"|trans([minimum_age], "contao_default") }}</p>
    {% endif %}

    {% if is_empty %}
        <p class="consho-cart__empty">{{ "CONSHO.cart.empty"|trans({}, "contao_default") }}</p>
    {% else %}
        {% if unpriced is not empty %}
            <p class="consho-cart__unpriced" role="alert">{{ "CONSHO.cart.unpriced"|trans({}, "contao_default") }}</p>
        {% endif %}

        {#
            ⚠️ The article is a <td>, not a <th scope="row">, and every cell
            carries data-cellheadline (C-10). Themes that turn a table
            into cards on a phone — the Contao demo theme among them — hide
            every <th> below the breakpoint and print attr(data-cellheadline)
            before each cell. A row header vanished there with the article
            name in it; the column headers stay for everything wider.
        #}
        {% set head_article = "CONSHO.cart.article"|trans({}, "contao_default") %}
        {% set head_quantity = "CONSHO.cart.quantity"|trans({}, "contao_default") %}
        {% set head_total = "CONSHO.cart.lineTotal"|trans({}, "contao_default") %}
        {% set head_actions = "CONSHO.cart.actions"|trans({}, "contao_default") %}
        <table class="consho-cart__lines">
            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th scope="col">{{ head_article }}</th>
                    <th scope="col">{{ head_quantity }}</th>
                    <th scope="col">{{ head_total }}</th>
                    <th scope="col"><span class="invisible">{{ head_actions }}</span></th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                {% for line in lines %}
                    {% set line_title = line.title ?: "CONSHO.cart.unknownArticle"|trans({}, "contao_default") %}
                    {% set line_mark = line.sku ? "CONSHO.detail.sku"|trans({}, "contao_default") ~ ' ' ~ line.sku : '#' ~ line.position %}
                    {% set line_name = line_title ~ ' (' ~ line_mark ~ ')' %}
                    {% set quantity_id = field_prefix ~ '-quantity-' ~ line.itemId %}
                    <tr>
                        <td data-cellheadline="{{ head_article }}">
                            {{ line_title }}
                            <span class="consho-cart__mark">{{ line_mark }}</span>
                            {#- The conditions of a subscription line (Abo-2, A10),
                               in the row rather than a tooltip: they are what the
                               line costs, not a detail about it. #}
                            {% if line.terms|default(null) %}
                                <br><small class="consho-cart__terms">{{ line.terms }}</small>
                            {% endif %}
                            {#- Abo-7b (P67): which subscription this line renews. #}
                            {% if line.renews|default('') %}
                                <br><small class="consho-cart__renews">{{ "CONSHO.cart.renews"|trans([line.renews], "contao_default") }}</small>
                            {% endif %}
                            {#- Block G (G5): the basket holds nothing back. #}
                            {% if line.stock|default(null) %}
                                {% if line.stock.short and line.stock.state == 'unavailable' %}
                                    <br><strong class="consho-cart__stock consho-cart__stock--short">{{ "CONSHO.stock.unavailable"|trans({}, "contao_default") }}</strong>
                                {% elseif line.stock.short %}
                                    <br><strong class="consho-cart__stock consho-cart__stock--short">{{ "CONSHO.stock.onlyLeft"|trans([line.stock.left], "contao_default") }}</strong>
                                {% elseif line.stock.state == 'backorder' %}
                                    <br><small class="consho-cart__stock">{{ "CONSHO.stock.backorder"|trans({}, "contao_default") }}</small>
                                {% endif %}
                            {% endif %}
                        </td>
                        <td data-cellheadline="{{ head_quantity }}">
                            {#- A renewal keeps the old quantity (A11):
                               shown, not a field. #}
                            {% if line.renews|default('') %}
                                {{ line.quantity }}
                            {% else %}
                            <form method="post" class="consho-cart__update">
                                <input type="hidden" name="REQUEST_TOKEN" value="{{ contao.request_token }}">
                                <input type="hidden" name="item" value="{{ line.itemId }}">

                                {#- The label names the line as well as the field: "Menge"
                                   on its own is the same accessible name in every row —
                                   and so is the title alone, for two lines of one product. #}
                                <label class="invisible" for="{{ quantity_id }}">
                                    {{ "CONSHO.cart.quantityOf"|trans([line_name], "contao_default") }}
                                </label>
                                <input
                                    id="{{ quantity_id }}"
                                    class="consho-cart__quantity"
                                    type="text"
                                    inputmode="decimal"
                                    name="quantity"
                                    value="{{ line.quantity }}"
                                >
                                <button type="submit" name="consho_cart_action" value="update">
                                    {{ "CONSHO.cart.update"|trans({}, "contao_default") }}<span class="invisible"> {{ line_name }}</span>
                                </button>
                            </form>
                            {% endif %}
                        </td>
                        <td data-cellheadline="{{ head_total }}">{{ line.lineGross }}</td>
                        <td data-cellheadline="{{ head_actions }}">
                            <form method="post" class="consho-cart__remove">
                                <input type="hidden" name="REQUEST_TOKEN" value="{{ contao.request_token }}">
                                <input type="hidden" name="item" value="{{ line.itemId }}">
                                <button type="submit" name="consho_cart_action" value="remove">
                                    {{ "CONSHO.cart.remove"|trans({}, "contao_default") }}<span class="invisible"> {{ line_name }}</span>
                                </button>
                            </form>
                        </td>
                    </tr>
                {% endfor %}

                {#- A line the pricer could not price: no price row left, or no tax
                   rate for its class in this country. It is shown WITH ITS NAME and
                   offers removal — without the name the visitor cannot tell which
                   of the buttons to press. No quantity field: a quantity that
                   cannot be priced is not worth correcting, only removing. #}
                {% for line in unpriced %}
                    {% set line_title = line.title ?: "CONSHO.cart.unknownArticle"|trans({}, "contao_default") %}
                    {% set line_mark = line.sku ? "CONSHO.detail.sku"|trans({}, "contao_default") ~ ' ' ~ line.sku : '#' ~ line.position %}
                    {% set line_name = line_title ~ ' (' ~ line_mark ~ ')' %}
                    <tr class="consho-cart__line--unpriced">
                        <td data-cellheadline="{{ head_article }}">
                            {{ line_title }}
                            <span class="consho-cart__mark">{{ line_mark }}</span>
                        </td>
                        <td data-cellheadline="{{ head_quantity }}">{{ line.quantity }}</td>
                        <td data-cellheadline="{{ head_total }}">{{ "CONSHO.cart.noPrice"|trans({}, "contao_default") }}</td>
                        <td data-cellheadline="{{ head_actions }}">
                            <form method="post" class="consho-cart__remove">
                                <input type="hidden" name="REQUEST_TOKEN" value="{{ contao.request_token }}">
                                <input type="hidden" name="item" value="{{ line.itemId }}">
                                <button type="submit" name="consho_cart_action" value="remove">
                                    {{ "CONSHO.cart.remove"|trans({}, "contao_default") }}<span class="invisible"> {{ line_name }}</span>
                                </button>
                            </form>
                        </td>
                    </tr>
                {% endfor %}
            </tbody>
            <tfoot>
                {#- Block H (H-4): the discount that applies — the goods, the
                    amount off, then the total below. Free shipping saves
                    nothing here yet: the shipping is chosen in the checkout. #}
                {% if discount|default(null) %}
                    {% if not discount.freeShipping %}
                        <tr class="consho-cart__subtotal">
                            <th scope="row" colspan="2">{{ "CONSHO.cart.discount.subtotal"|trans({}, "contao_default") }}</th>
                            <td colspan="2">{{ subtotal }}</td>
                        </tr>
                    {% endif %}
                    <tr class="consho-cart__discount">
                        <th scope="row" colspan="2">{{ discount.title }}{% if discount.code %} <span class="consho-cart__code">({{ discount.code }})</span>{% endif %}</th>
                        <td colspan="2">{{ discount.freeShipping ? "CONSHO.cart.discount.freeShipping"|trans({}, "contao_default") : discount.amount }}</td>
                    </tr>
                {% endif %}
                <tr>
                    <th scope="row" colspan="2">{{ "CONSHO.cart.total"|trans({}, "contao_default") }}</th>
                    <td colspan="2" data-cellheadline="{{ "CONSHO.cart.total"|trans({}, "contao_default") }}">
                        {{- total }}
                        {# Which of the two sentences appears is decided in the
                           controller and travels on showsNet (C-4). #}
                        <span class="consho-cart__tax">{{ untaxed|default(false) ? ((shipped ?? true) ? "CONSHO.priceShippingOnly"|trans({}, "contao_default") : "") : ("CONSHO." ~ ((shipped ?? true) ? "priceTaxNotice" : "priceTaxOnly") ~ (showsNet|default(false) ? "Net" : ""))|trans({}, "contao_default") }}</span>
                    </td>
                </tr>
            </tfoot>
        </table>

        {#- Block H (H-4, W1): the discount code. Typed, it stays on the basket
            and the line below says what became of it. #}
        {% if discount_enabled|default(false) %}
            <div class="consho-cart__discount-code">
                {% if discount_code|default('') %}
                    <form method="post">
                        <input type="hidden" name="REQUEST_TOKEN" value="{{ contao.request_token }}">
                        <p class="consho-cart__code-status consho-cart__code-status--{{ code_status }}" role="status">
                            {{ ("CONSHO.cart.discount.status." ~ code_status)|trans([discount_code, code_missing], "contao_default") }}
                        </p>
                        <button type="submit" name="consho_cart_action" value="removeCode">{{ "CONSHO.cart.discount.remove"|trans({}, "contao_default") }}</button>
                    </form>
                {% else %}
                    <form method="post">
                        <input type="hidden" name="REQUEST_TOKEN" value="{{ contao.request_token }}">
                        <label for="consho-discount-code">{{ "CONSHO.cart.discount.code"|trans({}, "contao_default") }}</label>
                        <input id="consho-discount-code" type="text" name="discount_code" maxlength="64" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false" autocapitalize="off">
                        <button type="submit" name="consho_cart_action" value="code">{{ "CONSHO.cart.discount.apply"|trans({}, "contao_default") }}</button>
                    </form>
                {% endif %}
            </div>
        {% endif %}

        {#- Wertgutscheine (WG-5, E3): several vouchers, each with what it
            holds or why it pays nothing; set against the total at the
            checkout, where the shipping is known. #}
        {% if voucher_enabled|default(false) %}
            <div class="consho-cart__vouchers">
                {% if vouchers|default([]) is not empty %}
                    <ul class="consho-cart__voucher-list">
                        {% for voucher in vouchers %}
                            <li class="consho-cart__voucher consho-cart__voucher--{{ voucher.status }}">
                                <form method="post">
                                    <input type="hidden" name="REQUEST_TOKEN" value="{{ contao.request_token }}">
                                    <input type="hidden" name="voucher" value="{{ voucher.value }}">
                                    <span role="status">{{ ("CONSHO.cart.voucher.status." ~ voucher.status)|trans([voucher.code, voucher.balance], "contao_default") }}</span>
                                    <button type="submit" name="consho_cart_action" value="removeVoucher" aria-label="{{ "CONSHO.cart.voucher.removeLabel"|trans([voucher.code], "contao_default") }}">{{ "CONSHO.cart.voucher.remove"|trans({}, "contao_default") }}</button>
                                </form>
                            </li>
                        {% endfor %}
                    </ul>
                {% endif %}
                {% if voucher_payable|default(false) %}
                    {% if vouchers|default([]) is not empty %}
                        <p class="consho-cart__voucher-later">{{ "CONSHO.cart.voucher.later"|trans({}, "contao_default") }}</p>
                    {% endif %}
                    <form method="post">
                        <input type="hidden" name="REQUEST_TOKEN" value="{{ contao.request_token }}">
                        <label for="consho-voucher-code">{{ "CONSHO.cart.voucher.code"|trans({}, "contao_default") }}</label>
                        <input id="consho-voucher-code" type="text" name="voucher_code" maxlength="32" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false" autocapitalize="characters">
                        <button type="submit" name="consho_cart_action" value="voucher">{{ "CONSHO.cart.voucher.apply"|trans({}, "contao_default") }}</button>
                    </form>
                {% else %}
                    <p class="consho-cart__voucher-later">{{ "CONSHO.cart.voucher.notForVouchers"|trans({}, "contao_default") }}</p>
                {% endif %}
            </div>
        {% endif %}

        {#- P12: the checkout will ask for an account — said before the link,
           not after the click. #}
        {% if account_required|default(false) %}
            <p class="consho-cart__account" role="note">{{ "CONSHO.subscription.accountRequired"|trans({}, "contao_default") }}</p>
        {% endif %}

        {% if checkout_url|default('') %}
            {#
                The way on (4.2). A link, not a form: going to the checkout
                changes nothing, and a GET may be repeated.
            #}
            <p class="consho-cart__checkout">
                <a href="{{ checkout_url }}" class="consho-cart__checkout-link">
                    {{ "CONSHO.cart.checkout"|trans({}, "contao_default") }}
                </a>
            </p>
        {% elseif checkout_blocked|default(false) %}
            {#- E4: the checkout is blocked — the sentence it would say, not a
               link to it. #}
            <p class="consho-cart__blocked" role="note">{{ "CONSHO.checkout.blocked"|trans({}, "contao_default") }}</p>
        {% endif %}
    {% endif %}
{% endblock %}
